# ## Study: REFRESH resuscitation protocols in severe sepsis (McDaniel et al. 2019, Figs 11-13) (`mcdaniel-2019-refresh`)
#
# **Question.** Do the paper's two REFRESH-trial protocols, liberal fluid boluses (control) and restricted fluid with norepinephrine (experimental), reach the resuscitation goals in the severe infection, with how much fluid, and what does a 12 h delay do to the control protocol (Fig 13)?
#
# **Objective.** Starting from the severe infection's state saved at 44 h, run biogears_sepsis (60 s updates) with treatment refresh_control and refresh_experimental (challenge at 44 h, antibiotic and protocol from 46 to 52 h), and refresh_control delayed by 12 h (challenge at 56 h, protocol from 58 to 64 h).
#
# **Hypothesis.** Both protocols raise SBP above 90 and MAP above 65 mmHg by the end of their 6 h; the experimental protocol does so with less saline than the control; the same control protocol started 12 h later meets a more hypotensive patient and gives more saline.

# ### Parameters
#
# | simulation | composite | steps | params |
# | --- | --- | --- | --- |
# | `refresh-control` | `viva_biogears.composites.sepsis.biogears_sepsis` | 480 | severity=severe, nutrition=infection_scenario, interval=60.0, treatment=refresh_control, state_file=StandardMale@severe-infection-44h.xml, n_steps=480 |

# ### The model & its parameters
#
# Each composite is a process-bigraph *document* — named processes wired by `inputs`/`outputs` ports over shared stores. Below, each composite shows what it does, then a **parameter cell** with its tunable knobs (the current default and what each one means). Edit any value, then re-run the **Run** section to rebuild and re-simulate with your changes.

# **The model — `viva_biogears.composites.sepsis.biogears_sepsis`**
#
# An infection in the real BioGears 8.2.0 engine (McDaniel et al. 2019): the acute inflammatory response, its clinical signs, the endothelial leak and lymph it drives, with BioGears' own meal and water schedule; emits every simulated minute by default.

# === Parameters — edit any value, then re-run from the Run cell below ===
# Each entry is the composite's current default; the comment explains it.
ov_viva_biogears_composites_sepsis_biogears_sepsis = {
    'severity'              : 'severe',   # Infection started at t = 0 ('none' for an uninfected control)
    'infection_location'    : 'Skin',   # Infection site (a label)
    'infection_mic_mg_per_L': 16.0,   # Pathogen minimum inhibitory concentration (the paper's 16 mg/L)
    'nutrition'             : 'infection_scenario',   # infection_scenario: BioGears' InfectionModerate schedule (water hourly, five meals in 48 h); none: no intake
    'iv_compound'           : 'Saline',   # IV fluid (the protocols' saline)
    'iv_rate_mL_per_min'    : 0.0,   # Infusion rate from t = 0 (no protocol only)
    'treatment'             : 'none',   # McDaniel et al. 2019 treatment protocol (viva_biogears.protocols): fluid_challenge (Fig 9), antibiotic (Fig 10), refresh_control and refresh_experimental (Figs 11-13); run to its end_h
    'challenge_h'           : 44.0,   # Saline challenge (2 x 500 mL) at
    'treatment_start_h'     : 46.0,   # Antibiotic and REFRESH start (58 for Fig 13's delayed arm)
    'treatment_duration_h'  : 6.0,   # REFRESH reassessment period
    'drug_readouts'         : None,   # Drugs whose concentrations are read (circuits/treatment/<drug>); default Piperacillin and Norepinephrine when treated, none otherwise. Give an untreated arm the treated arms' list to record the same stores
    'state_file'            : 'StandardMale@0s.xml',   # BioGears state in <runtime>/states or the package's states/ (or an absolute path)
    'patient_file'          : '',   # Patient file in <runtime>/patients (or a path), stabilized once (about 40 s) and then cached; replaces state_file
    'conditions'            : {},   # Chronic conditions applied while the patient stabilizes, e.g. {ChronicAnemia: {ReductionFactor: 0.3}}; with no patient_file, StandardMale.xml. A different patient, not a perturbation
    'circuit_additions'     : {},   # New path name -> {source, target, resistance_mmHg_s_per_mL}: a resistance path between two FullCardiovascular nodes in different vascular compartments, added with its compartment link so substances follow. A perturbation: the body responds over time
    'interval'              : 60.0,   # Seconds per update
    'time_step_s'           : 0.02,   # BioGears' solver step (validated at 0.02 s; must be < 0.1 s)
}

